Imports:
  - Types:
      - Logger
    From: BrowserKit/Sources/Common/Logger

Usages:
  subclass_pattern: |
    BaseCoordinator is the base class; roughly 15 concrete coordinators (one per navigation
    flow, e.g. a settings coordinator, a browser coordinator, a launch coordinator, a password
    manager coordinator, a Quick Answers coordinator) subclass it and override their own
    route-handling logic for exactly the routes that flow owns. A parent coordinator adds a
    child when starting a flow and removes it (typically once notified that the child's flow has
    finished) when that flow completes.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the navigation-coordinator pattern used throughout the app: each screen/flow owns
  a `Coordinator` that knows how to present itself and its children, so that navigation
  decisions live outside individual view controllers. A route value (defined in this same
  target's own routing subdirectory, out of scope for this cell) is what coordinators are asked
  to handle; the router (also out of scope here) is the thin navigation-controller-backed
  presentation primitive coordinators use to actually push/present.

  Use `subclass_pattern` when adding a new navigation flow.

---

"Coordinator()":
  location: Coordinator.swift
  annotations: |
    Contract every navigation-flow coordinator satisfies: identity, a child-coordinator list (the
    navigation graph is a tree), the router it presents through, and route handling.
  properties:
    "id -> UUID": |
      Unique identifier of this coordinator instance.
    "childCoordinators -> [Coordinator]": |
      Coordinators for sub-flows started by this one.
    "router -> Router": |
      Presentation primitive this coordinator pushes/presents view controllers through.
    "logger -> Logger": |
      Used to log navigation decisions.
    "isDismissible -> Bool": |
      Whether this coordinator can currently be dismissed (some flows must finish, e.g. while
      saving state, before they can be torn down).
    "savedRoute -> Route?": |
      A route this coordinator (or one of its children) could not yet handle, saved to retry
      once possible.
  methods:
    "handle(route: Route)": |
      Perform the navigation for the given route. Implemented per concrete coordinator; the base
      implementation does nothing.
    "canHandle(route: Route) -> canHandle:Bool": |
      Whether this coordinator (not its children) can handle the given route. Implemented per
      concrete coordinator; the base implementation returns false.
    "find(route: Route) -> coordinator:Coordinator?": |
      Recursively search this coordinator's own route-handling check and then its children for
      one that can handle the route.

      `coordinator`: the matching coordinator, or nil if none found (in which case the route is
      saved for a later retry)
    "findAndHandle(route: Route) -> coordinator:Coordinator?": |
      Find a coordinator for the route, dismiss any of its dismissible children first, then hand
      the route to it.

      `coordinator`: the coordinator that handled the route, or nil if none found
    "add(child: Coordinator)": |
      Register a child coordinator (starting a sub-flow).
    "remove(child: Coordinator?)": |
      Unregister a previously added child coordinator (ending a sub-flow).
    "removeAllChildren()": |
      Unregister every child coordinator.

"Coordinator::BaseCoordinator(router: Router, logger: Logger)":
  location: BaseCoordinator.swift
  annotations: |
    Default implementation of the whole `Coordinator` contract: manages the child-coordinator
    list, the saved route, and the recursive find/findAndHandle search; leaves the two
    route-handling checks for subclasses to override for their own routes.

    `router`: presentation primitive this coordinator pushes/presents through
    `logger`: diagnostic logger; defaults to the app-wide `Logger` singleton

    Use `subclass_pattern` for how concrete flow coordinators build on this.

"ParentCoordinatorDelegate()":
  location: ParentCoordinatorDelegate.swift
  annotations: |
    Implemented by a coordinator that starts child coordinators, so a finished child can signal
    its parent to remove it.
  methods:
    "didFinish(from childCoordinator: Coordinator)": |
      The given child coordinator's flow has completed and it should be torn down.

